{"id": "EUVD-2026-96602", "enisaUuid": "bd8092a7-f751-389f-8469-22e203efa555", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SysTenantController deleteApply handler that allows any authenticated user to reject tenant administrator applications. Low-privileged attackers can send PUT requests with chosen tenantId, packId and userId values to delete pending applications in any tenant and notify applicants of rejection.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:38:21", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_tenant_delete_apply.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysTenantController.java#L849-L853", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-tenant-deleteapply"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108663", "GHSA-6qfv-pf2c-5773"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "76f2af65-a950-304c-996c-2f259b98b4de", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0ba29077-cb68-305a-a844-345bbefa4e57", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}